# The Postgres init scripts run INSIDE a Linux container. A Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true would give them CRLF line endings, and the container's
# shell fails on the \r ("bad interpreter" / silent no-op) — so the databases
# would come up empty with no obvious cause. Force LF regardless of platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
